<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">First Empire of Haiti</h1><p class="st-meta">1804 CE – 1806 CE · capital Marchand-Dessalines</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first independent state created by formerly enslaved people, ruled by Emperor Jacques I, the revolutionary general Jean-Jacques Dessalines.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vertieres">Vertières</a> in November 1803, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a> proclaimed the independence of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-haiti">Haiti</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonaives">Gonaïves</a> on 1 January 1804, reviving the island's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> name. In September 1804 he took the title of emperor, in conscious rivalry with Napoleon, and was crowned as Jacques I in October.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Dessalines</a> ruled as a military autocrat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marchand-dessalines">Marchand</a>, his fortified capital in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artibonite">Artibonite</a>. In early 1804 he ordered the killing of most remaining French whites. The 1805 constitution banned white property ownership, declared all Haitians black and made the state the owner of much former plantation land. To revive exports, he forced labourers back onto plantations under military supervision, which caused growing resentment.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Land reviews that threatened the property of the mixed-race elite, combined with harsh labour rules, provoked a conspiracy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Dessalines</a> was ambushed and killed at Pont-Rouge near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-au-prince">Port-au-Prince</a> on 17 October 1806. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-haiti">Haiti</a> then split between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-christophe">Henri Christophe's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-haiti">State of Haiti</a> in the north and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Alexandre Pétion's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti-1806-1849">Republic of Haiti</a> in the south.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-empire-of-haiti.jpg" alt="First Empire of Haiti" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Saul ip Code cleanup by Mnmazur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Haiti_(1964%E2%80%931986,_civil).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1804 CE – 1806 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Marchand-Dessalines</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jacques I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism and Vodou</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Haitian Creole and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/haiti">Haiti</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Empire of Haiti (1804-1806), Haiti (1804-1806)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1805&amp;focus=first-empire-of-haiti" aria-label="First Empire of Haiti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2724 1470 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Empire of Haiti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3044 1726L3044 1726M3044 1726L3044 1726M3044 1726L3041 1746"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3044 1726h0M3044 1726h0M3041 1746h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3044 1726h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3044 1726h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1805&amp;focus=first-empire-of-haiti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
